  "live_records": {
    "q-224969": {
      "dom_id": "step-q224969",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(5.3)$ given below, compute $P(5\\le X\\le 8).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.2254\\,$ | $\\,0.3895\\,$ | $\\,0.5635\\,$ | $\\,0.7171\\,$ | $\\,0.8335\\,$ | $\\,0.9106\\,$ | $\\,0.9559\\,$ |\n\n$P(5\\le X\\le 8)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(8) & =P(X\\le 8) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,8\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\})+P(X\\in \\{5,6,7,8\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(5\\le X\\le 8) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(5\\le X\\le 8).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5\\le X\\le 8) & =F(8)-F(4) \\\\  & =0.9106-0.3895 \\\\  & =0.5211.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
