    "q-225080": {
      "dom_id": "step-q225080",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(2.7)$ given below, compute $P(X>7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.4936\\,$ | $\\,0.7141\\,$ | $\\,0.8629\\,$ | $\\,0.9433\\,$ | $\\,0.9794\\,$ | $\\,0.9934\\,$ | $\\,0.9981\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>7) & =1-P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =1-F(7) \\\\  & =1-0.9934 \\\\  & =0.0066.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
